<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liu Yu (Qi)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1073">1073</a>–1146</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Emperor of Da Qi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liu Yu was a former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> official who surrendered to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> Jin and was installed by them in 1130 as emperor of a puppet state called Qi, ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a>. He served as a buffer and attacked the Southern Song, but his campaigns failed. The Jin deposed him in 1137 and abolished his state.</p></div>
